libstdc++-internal by construction: __is_invocable is libstdc++'s <type_traits> struct template; libc++ defines no such name, and the real toolchain rejects this source (clang++ -std=c++20 -stdlib=libc++: "use of undeclared identifier '__is_invocable'"). The portable spelling (std::is_invocable_v) is the follow-up twin once the qualified variable-template constant fold (tmp/r49) lands; libc++'s own invocability machinery is exercised by the container tests in the lane.
